* SYSCMD_NATIVE_CREATE_IMPORT_v2 -- WITHDRAWN / DO NOT EXECUTE
* Status: INERT. Every operational line is deliberately commented out.
*
* WHY THIS WAS WITHDRAWN (2026-07-26):
* Drafted to seed 176 "missing" SYSCMD rows after the dotref generator reported
* 14.9% metadata coverage. That premise was WRONG.
*
* The generator defaults to reading the CSV snapshot
*   dottalkpp\data\scripts\metadata\SYSCMD_IMPORT_v1.csv   (40 rows, stale since 2026-05-20)
* but the CANONICAL table is
*   dottalkpp\data\metadata\SYSCMD.dbf                     (203 rows, already seeded)
*
* True coverage measured against the live table is 78.4% (200/255), not 14.9%.
*
* Executing this script would have:
*   1. ERASEd the canonical SYSCMD table, and
*   2. re-imported a 216-row CSV that OMITS 15 rows present in the live table:
*      BUILDLMDB, PREDHELP, SETPATH, WHERECACHE, STUDENTECHO, STUDENTHELLO,
*      SET CASE, SET CDX, SET CNX, SET FILTER, SET INDEX, SET NEAR,
